# ============================================================================
# Secrets — NEVER committed. (PROJECT_RULES.md Door 3 / secrets custody.)
# The most permanent secret in the system is the email-hash pepper; losing it
# de-joins all history, leaking it makes low-entropy addresses brute-forceable.
# It, node tokens, vendor keys, and Supabase keys are loaded from secure config
# at runtime and are never present in the repo. See config/secrets.example.env.
# ============================================================================
*.env
.env
.env.*
!*.example.env
# Secrets STORE directories (real key/pepper material) — a BROAD `**/secrets/` guard (defense in
# depth: catches extensionless / .json creds at ANY depth, which the *.pem/*.key/… rules below do
# NOT). The Go SOURCE package control-plane/internal/secrets/ is code (never secret material) and
# MUST be tracked or a fresh clone won't compile — so we re-include ONLY its *.go files: the dir is
# un-ignored so git descends into it, its contents are re-ignored, then only *.go is un-ignored.
# Net: a stray credential (service_account.json, a bare `token`) dropped in that package STAYS
# blocked; only source compiles into the repo. (The original unanchored `secrets/` swallowed the
# whole package silently — a fresh clone wouldn't build.)
**/secrets/
!/control-plane/internal/secrets/
/control-plane/internal/secrets/*
!/control-plane/internal/secrets/*.go
*.pem
*.key
*.pepper
config/secrets.env
config/local.*.yaml

# Go (control-plane)
/control-plane/bin/
/control-plane/dist/
*.test
*.out
coverage.txt
coverage.html

# Ruby (verifier-node / forked truemail-rack)
verifier-node/**/.bundle/
verifier-node/**/vendor/bundle/
verifier-node/**/tmp/
verifier-node/**/coverage/
verifier-node/**/log/
*.gem

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Build / CI artifacts
/artifacts/
/.task-cache/

# scratch dir of scripts/check-dns-search-domain.sh (removed on exit; ignored in case a run is killed)
.dns-fixture-work/
